GitOps vs Traditional Deployment

✨ Hello DevOps Learners!
Continuing my GitOps journey after completing Ansible, today I’m understanding how GitOps differs from traditional deployments and why modern companies are shifting towards it. 🚀
Let’s compare 👇

🔴 Traditional Deployment (Manual Approach)
Manual configuration changes on servers
Risk of human errors
Hard to track who changed what
Rollbacks are complex
Environment drift is common

🟢 GitOps Deployment (Modern Approach)
All changes go through Git (pull requests)
Automated deployment via controllers
Full version history & easy rollback
Continuous reconciliation prevents drift
Improved collaboration & auditability

💡 Real Industry Insight:**
 In production environments, manual changes often cause inconsistencies between Dev, Stage, and Prod. GitOps solves this by ensuring the cluster state always matches what is defined in Git.
That’s why many modern DevOps teams are adopting GitOps for reliability and scalability.
